bni SIGSEGVs on errors.Is over a user-defined errors.Error (tracked MAJOR)

The example's ParseError — a concrete error type carrying a line number — is
exactly the shape that crashes the bytecode VM: `errors.Is(err, base)` segfaults
when err's dynamic type implements errors.Error from user code. Reproduced on
released bnc-0.0.12 and on a main-built bnc-0.0.13-pre1 bundle; the same program
compiled with bnc is correct throughout.

So the interpreted leg of both this example's unit tests and its e2e harness
dies, and the whole example sits out the default sweeps rather than reddening
them. Everything still works compiled, and is run that way by hand:

    scripts/run-tests-compiled.sh errors/pkg/config     # 10 tests
    errors/tests/run.sh                                 # compiled vs fixture

Remove this file (and restore the interpreted leg in errors/tests/run.sh) once a
toolchain carrying the fix is pinned in BUILDER_VERSION.
